<% content_for :title, "Tooltip" %>

<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Overlays</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Tooltip</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    A short text hint for a control, shown on hover and on keyboard focus: the name of an icon-only button, or what a
    shortcut does. It is read as the control's description, paints above dialogs and menus without closing them, and stays
    on screen near a viewport edge. Like Popover, it's here for the browser behaviour, not for anything Rails-specific.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-background flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-6 p-12 mb-8">
  <% [["top", "Top"], ["bottom", "Bottom"], ["left", "Left"], ["right", "Right"]].each do |placement, label| %>
    <%= render Ui::TooltipComponent.new(text: "Tooltip #{label.downcase}", placement: placement) do |t| %>
      <% t.with_trigger do %>
        <button class="rounded-md border border-input bg-background px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground transition-colors">
          <%= label %>
        </button>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#tooltip-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed"><code id="tooltip-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_tooltip_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["text",      "String",  "required", "The tooltip text content."],
        ["placement", "String or Symbol", '"top"', "One of: top, top-start, top-end, bottom, bottom-start, bottom-end, left, left-start, left-end, right, right-start, right-end. :bottom_start works as well as \"bottom-start\"."],
        ["offset",    "Integer", "6",        "Gap in pixels between the trigger and the tooltip."],
        ["class",     "String",  "nil",      "Merged onto the tooltip's root element, which wraps the trigger."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Slots</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-start px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary">trigger</td>
        <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground">The element that receives hover and focus events to show the tooltip.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Accessibility</h2>
<ul class="text-sm text-muted-foreground space-y-2 mb-8 list-disc ps-5">
  <li>The control in the trigger slot gets <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-describedby</code> pointing at the tooltip, which has
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role="tooltip"</code>. The tooltip describes the control; it doesn't name it, so an icon-only button still needs
      <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-label</code>.</li>
  <li>It shows on focus as well as hover, and stays while either lasts. The pointer can travel onto the tooltip without it
      disappearing.</li>
  <li>Escape hides it without moving focus, and without closing a dialog the control sits in.</li>
  <li>A native <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">disabled</code> control never receives focus, so keyboard and screen reader users can't reach its
      tooltip even though a mouse can. If a disabled control needs one, use <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">aria-disabled="true"</code> instead, so it
      stays focusable.</li>
</ul>

<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">When not to use it</h2>
<p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8">
  Anything a user needs to read to use the page belongs on the page, not behind a hover: a touch screen has no hover. Content
  with a link, a button or more than a sentence is a <%= link_to "Popover", popover_path, class: "text-primary underline" %>.
  Help text for a form field is a <%= link_to "Field", field_path, class: "text-primary underline" %> description.
</p>
